\f0\b \cf2 Comparators - Dynamic Ranges
\f1\b0 \
\
- having covered static ranges, what about dynamic ranges?\
- a mixture of the techniques above will need to be used.\
- In the simplest form, a dynamic range has, say, a fixed upper bound and a lower bound that can move and you can determine whether you are in the range by testing for each boundary condition separately and ANDing the result. \
